# Target C: monotone virtual-empty audit criterion

Date: 2026-09-27

For the eight-no-root `k=4, D=-1, d_root=0, p=3`, three-singleton `r=0` certificate, the support tag `tau_b` may underestimate the true local rank. The certificate remains valid because every actual-empty block still passes the eligibility predicate and the subsequent search only enlarges the virtual-empty family.

General criterion: if an inexact local tag is used only to form a superset of all possible actual-empty blocks, and every later test becomes weaker when virtual-empty blocks are added, then underestimating the local rank cannot cause a false exclusion. Here adding virtual empties shrinks the forced-complete set, preserves complete-row independence automatically, and increases the available face-local quotient capacity.

This criterion does not cover verifiers that use the underestimated rank to strengthen pairwise compatibility, increase a required local generator dimension, or reject selected-singleton placements. Those cases require separate audits.
